@startuml resolve-and-reopen
title US-13: Resolve and Recurrence - Terminal Resolution Creates New Incident on Recurrence

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Operator
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts" as TSDB
participant "Alert\nEvaluator" as Evaluator
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

Operator -> Dashboard : Resolve active alert
Dashboard -> API : PATCH /alerts/{alert_id}\n{ status: RESOLVED }
API -> TSDB : UPDATE alert\nSET status=RESOLVED, resolved_at=..., resolved_by=...
TSDB --> API : durable terminal state
API --> Dashboard : lifecycle update
Dashboard --> Operator : alert shown as RESOLVED

note over TSDB
  RESOLVED is terminal.
  The row is never reopened or overwritten.
end note

== Later, a new anomaly episode occurs ==

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish alert with new deterministic\nepisode/window identity
Kafka -> API : consume new logical alert
API -> TSDB : INSERT new alert row\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING
TSDB --> API : new NEW incident
API --> Dashboard : push new alert lifecycle event
Dashboard --> Operator : new incident displayed separately

note over Operator, TSDB
  Historical filename retained for link stability.
  Behavior is recurrence, not reopen.
end note

@enduml
